#: src/guides/highlights.md:1
msgid "Adding highlight queries"
msgstr ""

#: src/guides/highlights.md:3
msgid ""
"`highlights.scm` queries assign a highlight scope (`@function`, `@type`, "
"`@keyword`, ...) to nodes in the syntax tree; the theme then maps each scope "
"to a colour. Highlighting is the one query file that every language needs."
msgstr ""

#: src/guides/highlights.md:7
msgid ""
"Query files should be placed in `runtime/queries/{language}/highlights.scm` "
"when contributing to Helix."
msgstr ""

#: src/guides/highlights.md:10
msgid "Scopes"
msgstr ""

#: src/guides/highlights.md:12
msgid ""
"The full list of highlight scopes, and what each is for, is documented on "
"the [themes page](https://docs.helix-editor.com/themes.html#scopes). Match "
"the most specific scope that fits the node — for example a method call is "
"`@function.method` while a plain field access is `@variable.other.member`."
msgstr ""

#: src/guides/highlights.md:17
msgid ""
"A query file may reuse another language's with `; inherits: <lang>` on the "
"first line (for example `tsx` inherits `typescript`, which inherits `ecma`). "
"An inherited file is compiled against _each_ inheriting grammar, so every "
"capture must be valid there too."
msgstr ""

#: src/guides/highlights.md:22
msgid "Precedence"
msgstr ""

#: src/guides/highlights.md:24
msgid ""
"Two rules decide which capture wins when more than one matches the same text:"
msgstr ""

#: src/guides/highlights.md:26
msgid ""
"**Same span: last match wins.** Among captures covering the same bytes, the "
"pattern that appears later in the file wins. Put a generic rule _before_ the "
"specific one that should override it."
msgstr ""

#: src/guides/highlights.md:29
msgid ""
"**Nested nodes: innermost wins.** When a parent and a child node both cover "
"the text, the child's capture wins, regardless of file order."
msgstr ""

#: src/guides/highlights.md:32
msgid ""
"A common consequence of rule 2: capture the _leaf_ you mean. A call captured "
"on a wrapping node loses to a base `(identifier) @variable` on the inner "
"identifier, so put `@function` on the identifier itself."
msgstr ""

#: src/guides/highlights.md:36
msgid ""
"Where the grammar can't distinguish a scope, casing is often used as a "
"heuristic:"
msgstr ""

#: src/guides/highlights.md:40
msgid "\"^[A-Z][A-Z_]*$\""
msgstr ""

#: src/guides/highlights.md:43
msgid "Testing"
msgstr ""

#: src/guides/highlights.md:45
msgid ""
"`cargo xtask query-check [language]` confirms the queries are valid against "
"the grammar. `cargo xtask highlight-check [language]` runs the real "
"highlighter over the fixtures in `tests/query/highlights/<language-id>/"
"<name>.<ext>`, where a caret comment line (`// ^ @capture`) asserts the "
"winning scope at the column above it; this catches the precedence mistakes "
"that `query-check` cannot see. `cargo xtask highlight-check --dump "
"<language> <file>` prints the winning capture per span for an arbitrary file."
msgstr ""
